sub1("It failed, reproducing the committed feature on 36% of Pittsburgh and 82% of Delaware recordings, and the diagnosis proceeded by elimination: pronoun counts matched the committed values almost exactly (r = 0.9995 in both cohorts), so the tagger was not the problem; the committed Delaware extractor re-run on forty of its own inputs reproduced its committed output to the last digit, so environment drift was not the problem — the step that matters, because without it the comfortable conclusion would have been a library version; and reading the committed source line by line found that `linguistic_features.py:48` filters `words = [t for t in doc if t.is_alpha]` and the new script did not, so punctuation, contraction fragments and numerals were inflating the denominator. The defect was in the new script, measured against its own registered definition; fixing it honoured the registration, and after the fix the check passes at 100% in both cohorts. One cohort's result block had appeared in terminal output by then, which is recorded in the driver's registration history in those words, with the reasons it does not void the run — the fix was determined by reading the committed source rather than by the result, and no criterion or threshold moved — and with the sentence *the reader is entitled to weigh that*.",
     "It failed, reproducing the committed feature on 36% of Pittsburgh and 82% of Delaware recordings, and the diagnosis proceeded by elimination: pronoun counts matched the committed values almost exactly (r = 0.9995 in both cohorts), so the tagger was not the problem; the committed Delaware extractor re-run on forty of its own inputs reproduced its committed output to the last digit, so environment drift was not the problem — the step that matters, since without it the comfortable conclusion would have been a library version; and reading the committed source line by line found that `linguistic_features.py:48` filters `words = [t for t in doc if t.is_alpha]` and the new script did not, so punctuation, contraction fragments and numerals were inflating the denominator. The defect was in the new script; fixing it honoured the registration, and after the fix the check passes at 100% in both cohorts. One cohort's result block had appeared in terminal output by then, which the driver's registration history records in those words, with the reasons it does not void the run — the fix was determined by reading the committed source rather than by the result, and no criterion or threshold moved — and with the sentence *the reader is entitled to weigh that*.")
