sub1("Pre-registration in work of this kind is revised on contact with data considerably more often than the published literature suggests, because what gets published is the registrations that held. The discipline that matters is therefore not *never amend* but four rules that can be kept. First, never adjust the rule to reach the assertion: the retention criterion was left standing and uninterpretable rather than rewritten into something that would have graded cleanly. Second, record when an amendment was made relative to seeing the result, in the words a sceptical reader would use. Third, report both versions whenever an amendment changes an answer, as the task-count analysis does for its two label rules. Fourth, register a sanity gate on every derived quantity an analysis depends on, including its labels: the tokenisation defect was caught by exactly such a gate, the label defect was not caught because no gate had been placed on the labels, and every registration written after that episode carries one. The comparison defect extends the fourth rule from derived quantities to comparisons: register how each side of every comparison was arrived at, and refuse any comparison whose two sides were produced by procedures with different numbers of free parameters.",
     "Pre-registration in work of this kind is revised on contact with data more often than the published literature suggests, because what gets published is the registrations that held; the discipline that matters is therefore not *never amend* but four rules that can be kept. First, never adjust the rule to reach the assertion: the retention criterion was left standing and uninterpretable rather than rewritten into something that would have graded cleanly. Second, record when an amendment was made relative to seeing the result, in the words a sceptical reader would use. Third, report both versions whenever an amendment changes an answer, as the task-count analysis does for its two label rules. Fourth, register a sanity gate on every derived quantity an analysis depends on, including its labels: the tokenisation defect was caught by such a gate, the label defect was not because no gate had been placed on the labels, and every registration written after that episode carries one. The comparison defect extends the fourth rule to comparisons: register how each side was arrived at, and refuse any comparison whose two sides were produced by procedures with different numbers of free parameters.")

